# AI IDEAS:
#  27:35 "oh, Dan, I don't have the money for $30 a pound on salmon every week": EXCUSE VOICE, lip-synced. A middle class dad in a polo at a grocery seafood counter stares at the salmon price tag and whines the line to camera, his cart behind him piled with chips, soda and a 30 rack. The cart is the joke: the money is there. It is the only excuse voice in this stretch that is said to "you middle class people".
